The desk is where books go out and come back. It listens for scans all the time, so you rarely need
to click.

**You need:** a role with **Circulation desk**, **Check out & renew** and **Check in returns**,
normally the librarian. Open **Library → Circulation Desk**.

**Hardware:** a USB or Bluetooth barcode scanner set to Code 128 or Code 39 with an Enter suffix, and
a USB RFID reader in keyboard mode that reads the same cards as your gate readers. Without either,
use the camera: **Scan with camera** works on a phone, a tablet or a laptop webcam.

## Lend a book

1. **Tap the borrower's card.** The screen shows their name, their books on loan with due dates,
   holds and fines, and whether they may borrow another.
2. **Scan each book's barcode.** Each book is lent with the due date from the loan rules.
3. Select **Done**, or wait. The borrower closes by itself after the idle time in Library Settings.

A due date that falls on a closed day moves to the next school day. A double scan of the same book
is harmless.

If the card has no match, or a scan matches more than one thing, the desk says so
(**That scan matches more than one thing**). Look the person up by name instead. If **Lend only on a
card tap** is on, that needs an override.

## Return a book

Scan the book. You do not need to open the borrower first. If the book is late, the fine is worked
out and, when fines are on, charged at that moment. A second scan of an already returned book does
nothing. If the book has someone waiting, it goes to the hold shelf: see [Holds](/docs/educonnect-library-holds).

**Damaged?** On a return, record damage to charge for it.

## Renew

Renew from the borrower's list. A book with someone waiting for it is not renewed, and renewals stop
at the limit in the loan rules.

## When a book is on loan to someone else

Scanning it for a new borrower shows **This book is on loan to someone else**. Choose **Check in and
lend** if it has really come back.

## Overrides

A borrower at their limit, blocked, or owing too much cannot borrow. Someone with **Override** can
lend anyway: you must give a reason, and the desk shows **Override on: reason** until you finish.
Every override is recorded.

## Loans & Overdue

**Library → Loans & Overdue** has three lists: **All on loan**, **Overdue**, and **Returned today**.
Late books show the fine they would carry if returned today. That is a projection and nothing is
charged until the book comes back.

## Declare a book lost

Open the loan from the borrower's page and declare it lost. A student is charged the copy's price,
or the title's price, or the default replacement cost in settings, plus the lost processing fee. If
the book later turns up and is checked in, its unpaid fine is voided.

